API ENDPOINTS SPECIFICATION FOR DOCUTRACK PRO SYSTEM
Base URL Configuration

Base URL: https://your-api-gateway-id.execute-api.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/prod

1. AUTHENTICATION ENDPOINTS
1.1 User Registration

    Method: POST
    Path: /auth/register
    Description: Register a new user in the system
    Request Body:

{
  "email": "string",
  "password": "string", 
  "firstName": "string",
  "lastName": "string",
  "role": "user | processing-staff | deputy-director",
  "organization": "string (optional)",
  "department": "string (optional)"
}

    Response:
        Success (201): User registration confirmation
        Error (400): User already exists or validation error

1.2 User Login

    Method: POST
    Path: /auth/login
    Description: Authenticate user and return JWT token
    Request Body:

{
  "email": "string",
  "password": "string"
}

    Response:
        Success (200): User data and JWT token
        Error (401): Invalid credentials

2. DOCUMENT MANAGEMENT ENDPOINTS
2.1 Get All Documents

    Method: GET
    Path: /documents
    Description: Retrieve all documents accessible to the authenticated user
    Headers: Authorization: Bearer <token>
    Response:
        Success (200): Array of document objects
        Error (401): Unauthorized access

2.2 Create New Document

    Method: POST
    Path: /documents
    Description: Upload and create a new document
    Headers: Authorization: Bearer <token>
    Request Body:

{
  "name": "string",
  "content": "string",
  "clientName": "string",
  "department": "string",
  "priority": "low | medium | high",
  "deadline": "YYYY-MM-DD"
}

    Response:
        Success (201): Created document details
        Error (400): Validation error

2.3 Get Specific Document

    Method: GET
    Path: /documents/{documentId}
    Description: Retrieve details of a specific document
    Headers: Authorization: Bearer <token>
    Response:
        Success (200): Document details
        Error (404): Document not found

2.4 Update Document

    Method: PUT
    Path: /documents/{documentId}
    Description: Update document information and status
    Headers: Authorization: Bearer <token>
    Request Body:

{
  "name": "string (optional)",
  "content": "string (optional)",
  "status": "assigned | in-progress | completed",
  "priority": "low | medium | high"
}

    Response:
        Success (200): Update confirmation
        Error (404): Document not found

2.5 Delete Document

    Method: DELETE
    Path: /documents/{documentId}
    Description: Remove document from the system
    Headers: Authorization: Bearer <token>
    Response:
        Success (200): Deletion confirmation
        Error (404): Document not found

3. NOTIFICATION ENDPOINTS
3.1 Get User Notifications

    Method: GET
    Path: /notifications
    Query Parameters: userId=string
    Description: Retrieve notifications for a specific user
    Headers: Authorization: Bearer <token>
    Response:
        Success (200): Array of notification objects
        Error (401): Unauthorized access

3.2 Create Notification

    Method: POST
    Path: /notifications
    Description: Create a new notification
    Headers: Authorization: Bearer <token>
    Request Body:

{
  "type": "document_processed | document_edited | document_approved | document_rejected | document_assigned | deadline_reminder",
  "title": "string",
  "message": "string",
  "documentId": "string",
  "documentName": "string",
  "fromUser": "string",
  "toUser": "string"
}

    Response:
        Success (201): Notification created
        Error (400): Validation error

3.3 Mark Notification as Read

    Method: PUT
    Path: /notifications/{notificationId}
    Description: Mark a specific notification as read
    Headers: Authorization: Bearer <token>
    Response:
        Success (200): Update confirmation
        Error (404): Notification not found

4. REPORTING ENDPOINTS
4.1 Generate Analytics Report

    Method: GET
    Path: /reports
    Query Parameters: type=analytics
    Description: Generate comprehensive analytics report
    Headers: Authorization: Bearer <token>
    Response:
        Success (200): Report data or PDF URL
        Error (401): Unauthorized access

4.2 Generate Processing Report

    Method: GET
    Path: /reports
    Query Parameters: type=processing
    Description: Generate staff processing performance report
    Headers: Authorization: Bearer <token>
    Response:
        Success (200): Report data or PDF URL
        Error (401): Unauthorized access

4.3 Generate Custom Report

    Method: POST
    Path: /reports/custom
    Description: Generate custom report based on parameters
    Headers: Authorization: Bearer <token>
    Request Body:

{
  "reportType": "string",
  "dateRange": {
    "startDate": "YYYY-MM-DD",
    "endDate": "YYYY-MM-DD"
  },
  "filters": {
    "department": "string (optional)",
    "status": "string (optional)",
    "priority": "string (optional)"
  }
}

    Response:
        Success (200): Custom report data
        Error (400): Invalid parameters

5. SYSTEM HEALTH AND MONITORING ENDPOINTS
5.1 Health Check

    Method: GET
    Path: /health
    Description: Check system health and connectivity
    Response:
        Success (200): System status OK
        Error (503): System unavailable

5.2 System Statistics

    Method: GET
    Path: /system/stats
    Description: Get system usage statistics
    Headers: Authorization: Bearer <token> (Admin only)
    Response:
        Success (200): System statistics
        Error (403): Insufficient permissions

6. USER MANAGEMENT ENDPOINTS (Admin/Deputy Director)
6.1 Get All Users

    Method: GET
    Path: /users
    Description: Retrieve all system users (Admin only)
    Headers: Authorization: Bearer <token>
    Response:
        Success (200): Array of user objects
        Error (403): Insufficient permissions

6.2 Update User Role

    Method: PUT
    Path: /users/{userId}/role
    Description: Update user role (Admin only)
    Headers: Authorization: Bearer <token>
    Request Body:

{
  "role": "user | processing-staff | deputy-director"
}

    Response:
        Success (200): Update confirmation
        Error (403): Insufficient permissions

7. WORKFLOW MANAGEMENT ENDPOINTS
7.1 Get Workflow Status

    Method: GET
    Path: /workflow/{documentId}
    Description: Get current workflow status for a document
    Headers: Authorization: Bearer <token>
    Response:
        Success (200): Workflow status details
        Error (404): Document not found

7.2 Advance Workflow

    Method: POST
    Path: /workflow/{documentId}/advance
    Description: Move document to next workflow stage
    Headers: Authorization: Bearer <token>
    Request Body:

{
  "action": "approve | reject | return",
  "comments": "string (optional)"
}

    Response:
        Success (200): Workflow updated
        Error (400): Invalid workflow action

8. ERROR HANDLING

All endpoints return standardized error responses:

{
  "success": false,
  "error": "Error message",
  "code": "ERROR_CODE",
  "timestamp": "ISO 8601 timestamp"
}

9. AUTHENTICATION REQUIREMENTS

    All endpoints except /auth/register, /auth/login, and /health require JWT authentication
    JWT tokens should be included in the Authorization header as Bearer <token>
    Tokens expire after 24 hours and require renewal
    Role-based access control is enforced on protected endpoints

10. RATE LIMITING

    Authentication endpoints: 5 requests per minute per IP
    Document operations: 100 requests per minute per user
    Report generation: 10 requests per hour per user
    General API calls: 1000 requests per hour per user
